{title: 059 - Great Our Joy as Now We Gather}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #059 • MICHAEL • 8.8.8.7.6.7}
{lyricist: Fred Pratt Green}
{composer: Herbert Howells}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 59}
{meta: tune MICHAEL}
{meta: meter 8.8.8.7.6.7}
{meta: category Worship - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Great our [Am/C]joy as [F]now we gather
[Am]Where [C]the [Gm]Master [Am]makes [F]us [Gm]one:
[Am]Where [F]we [Am]worship [Edim]God [F]the [C]Father
[C]Thro' the [Am]Spirit [C]of [Am]His Son.
[Bb]All [Am]who [Gm]search [F]for His [Gm]church
[Gm]Find it where His [F]will is done.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Precious [Am/C]is the [F]tie that binds us
[Am]To [C]our [Gm]God when [Am]faith [Gm]grows [F]cold;
[Am]Precious all that [Edim]now [F]reminds [C/E]us
[C]He is [Am]still [Dm]our [C]safe [Am]stronghold.
[Bb]Faithful [Gm]love [F]serves to [Gm]prove
[Gm]Here the Shepherd [F]has His fold.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]May we [Am/C]learn from [F]Christ's example
[Am]How [C]to [Gm]use this [Am]house [Gm]of [F]prayer:
[Am]He [F]who [Am]loved and [Edim]cleansed [F]His [C]temple
[C]Wants us [Am]all [Dm]to [C]worship [Am]there.
[Bb]God [Am]the [Gm]Son [F]shuts out [Gm]none:
[Gm]In His Kingdom [F]all may share.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]Lord, inspire [Am]us [F]with Your vision
[Am]Of [C]a [Gm]world which [Am]must [Gm]be [F]won!
[Am]Glorious is [Gm]the [Edim]church's [Gm]mission,
[C]Long endeavored, scarce [Am]begun!
[Bb]Faithful [Gm]now- [F]this is [Gm]how
[Gm]God's eternal [F]will is done.
{end_of_verse}
